  "vibe": "Slate gym wall (#2c2f33) under safety-orange holds (#ff8a3d) and crash-pad blue (#3d7bff), everything set in Anton and locked to uppercase on every single beat. The backdrop is a bouldering wall: an overhang wedge cut out of the right edge, five differently-shaped holds popping in on an outBack stagger — jug, crimp, triangle sloper, oval pinch, curved pinch — a chalk puff blooming and fading off one of them, a rope swaying on a sine into an orange belay ring, and four blue pads laid down the floor. It owns the keycap mechanic: oversized keys physically depress with a squashing bottom edge, then a payoff word pops. Camera cadence 7 with 0.9 roll and 3° skew — the hardest-cutting pack in this set, defaulting to Bouncy. Built for climbing gyms, training apps, session trackers and any brand that sells effort.",
